# Build context exclusions.
#
# The images carry the application and the data it reads at startup, and nothing
# else. Two of these lines matter beyond image size:
#
#   .venv/          a host virtualenv copied into the context would shadow the
#                   image's own interpreter's site-packages if it were ever put
#                   on the path, and it carries host-absolute shebangs.
#   .env            the deployment's real secrets. Compose delivers them per
#                   service at runtime; a copy in a layer is a published secret
#                   that survives every `docker history` and every push.
#
# Everything else here is weight or noise: the suite, the review documents, the
# scratch trees, and the data directories, which are bind mounts at runtime and
# are never baked in.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore

.venv
venv
*.egg-info
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

node_modules
frontend/dist

tests
docs
scratchpad
PLAN.md
handoff.md
README.md
LICENSE

.env
*.log

# Runtime state. These are bind mounts from ${DATA_ROOT} on the deployment host;
# a copy in the image would be a stale map that silently shadows nothing and
# costs gigabytes.
data
tiles
postgres-data
dist
build
